{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And the woman was taken, and for Abram it went well.</b> They did not first consult him to persuade him, as was the custom, for they thought there was no need for that at all — since the king had taken her for a wife, and since she said only that she was Abram's sister and was fit to be married. No marriage would have been more distinguished than being taken by the king as a wife, as he testified in saying <b>And I took her for myself for a wife</b>. But they took her to the king first, and afterward the king dealt well <b>for her sake</b>, with a bride-price and gifts, as is the custom." "<b>Sheep and cattle and servants.</b> Abundant, as befits a king."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:29:56.499751503Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}